sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor K as Bruger (signed in)
    participant PM as ProfileModel
    participant US as IUserAccountStore
    participant DB as MarsvinDb
    participant AP as Authenticator app

    Note over K,AP: Optional second factor. Enrollment has two steps on purpose -<br/>a secret exists before 2FA is switched on, so nobody is locked out<br/>by a QR code they never scanned.

    K->>PM: POST Profile?handler=StartTotpEnrollment
    PM->>PM: Totp.GenerateSecret()<br/>20 random bytes, Base32
    PM->>US: SetTotpSecret(userId, secret)
    US->>US: encrypt with IDataProtector
    US->>DB: UPDATE Users SET TotpSecret = ciphertext, TotpEnabled = 0
    PM-->>K: Redirect to /Account/Profile

    K->>PM: GET /Account/Profile
    PM->>US: FindById(userId)
    US-->>PM: user with a pending secret, TotpEnabled = false
    PM->>PM: BuildOtpAuthUri(secret, email)<br/>QrCode.ToDataUri(uri)
    PM-->>K: QR code + secret in text form

    K->>AP: scans the QR code
    AP-->>K: 6-digit code, new every 30 seconds

    K->>PM: POST Profile?handler=ConfirmTotp (code)
    PM->>US: FindById(userId)
    PM->>PM: Totp.ValidateCode(secret, code)
    alt wrong code
        PM-->>K: Redirect with error "Forkert kode"
        Note over PM: TotpEnabled stays false,<br/>login is unchanged.
    else code ok
        PM->>US: SetTotpEnabled(userId, true)
        US->>DB: UPDATE Users SET TotpEnabled = 1
        PM-->>K: toast "2FA er nu aktiveret"
    end

    Note over K,DB: From the next login on, a correct password goes straight to<br/>/Account/VerifyTotp instead of sending an email link.

    K->>PM: POST Profile?handler=DisableTotp (currentPassword)
    PM->>PM: verify the current password
    alt wrong password
        PM-->>K: error, 2FA stays on
    else password ok
        PM->>US: SetTotpSecret(userId, null)
        US->>DB: UPDATE Users SET TotpSecret = NULL, TotpEnabled = 0
        PM-->>K: toast "2FA er deaktiveret"
    end
